<mq:insertedmatch matchtype="0" source="ローカルごった煮 / user" matchrate="100" originalmatchrate="0" ambiguousexact="false" setsegmentswhensplittingintorows="false" hitfororiginalsegementversion="false"><source xml:space="preserve"><bpt id="1" rid="1">&lt;mq:rxt displaytext=&quot;&amp;lt;h2&amp;gt;&quot; val=&quot;&amp;lt;h2&amp;gt;&quot;&gt;</bpt>Key Features of This Function<ept id="2" rid="1">&lt;/mq:rxt displaytext=&quot;&amp;lt;/h2&amp;gt;&quot; val=&quot;&amp;lt;/h2&amp;gt;&quot;&gt;</ept></source>
<target xml:space="preserve"><bpt id="3" rid="2">&lt;mq:rxt displaytext=&quot;&amp;lt;h2&amp;gt;&quot; val=&quot;&amp;lt;h2&amp;gt;&quot;&gt;</bpt>この機能の主な特徴<ept id="4" rid="2">&lt;/mq:rxt displaytext=&quot;&amp;lt;/h2&amp;gt;&quot; val=&quot;&amp;lt;/h2&amp;gt;&quot;&gt;</ept></target>
</mq:insertedmatch>
</mq:historical-unit>
<mq:historical-unit mq:minorversionend="1" mq:minorversionstart="1" mq:status="NotStarted" mq:segmentguid="e2a40a25-12b2-43ab-8e12-12d6d896aff2" mq:lastchangedtimestamp="2026-01-10T15:20:12Z" mq:lastchanginguser="user" mq:maxlengthchars="-1" mq:nosplitjoin="true" mq:firstlabel="0" mq:lastlabel="0" mq:autosplitjoinstate="0" mq:lastmodifrole="0" mq:multipleexactmatch="false">
<source xml:space="preserve" mq:segpart="0" mq:hasfollowingobject="hasfollowingobject">&lt;h2&gt;Key Features of This Function&lt;/h2&gt;<ph id="1">&lt;mq:ch val=&quot;
&quot; /&gt;</ph><ph id="2">&lt;mq:ch val=&quot;
&quot; /&gt;</ph>&lt;p&gt;In &lt;b&gt;multilingual texts&lt;/b&gt; such as videogame store descriptions, segment splitting is often &lt;b&gt;disabled in CAT tools&lt;/b&gt; to preserve cross-language alignment.&lt;/p&gt;<ph id="3">&lt;mq:ch val=&quot;
&quot; /&gt;</ph><ph id="4">&lt;mq:ch val=&quot;
&quot; /&gt;</ph>&lt;p&gt;As a result, translators are forced to work with &lt;b&gt;overly long and complex segments&lt;/b&gt; that mix multiple sentences or ideas.&lt;/p&gt;<ph id="5">&lt;mq:ch val=&quot;
&quot; /&gt;</ph><ph id="6">&lt;mq:ch val=&quot;
&quot; /&gt;</ph>&lt;p&gt;This function allows &lt;b&gt;safe external splitting&lt;/b&gt; of such segments while keeping the original &lt;b&gt;structural integrity&lt;/b&gt; required by CAT tools.&lt;/p&gt;<ph id="7">&lt;mq:ch val=&quot;
&quot; /&gt;</ph><ph id="8">&lt;mq:ch val=&quot;
&quot; /&gt;</ph>&lt;p&gt;Each split segment remains &lt;b&gt;traceable to its original context&lt;/b&gt;, ensuring that &lt;b&gt;merge operations&lt;/b&gt; can reliably reconstruct the source file.&lt;/p&gt;<ph id="9">&lt;mq:ch val=&quot;
&quot; /&gt;</ph><ph id="10">&lt;mq:ch val=&quot;
&quot; /&gt;</ph>&lt;p&gt;The feature is designed for scenarios where &lt;b&gt;different languages require different sentence boundaries&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</source>
<target xml:space="preserve"></target>
<mq:startingws xml:space="preserve" />
<mq:endingws xml:space="preserve" />
